      "id": 72915,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-09-09T11:01:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Damage types are Melée, Fire, Sonic, etc. Irreducible is an attribute which can be applied to damage (regardless of type). It mean cards like Fortitude and Ta Moko are of no use, because they reduce damage, so if that hero gets hit with irreducible damage, it ignores their protection. This does make Omni-10 good against Plague Rat, though, if you can get out the Ablative Coating and Reactive Plating Subroutine ASAP :).</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:52:28.587Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
