      "id": 72918,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-09-09T19:41:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Yeah, he can hit any target. So if he's Infected, he hits himself for irreducible toxic damage, and due to having the Ablative Coating (melée, projectile, toxic) and Reactive Plating Subroutine out, he then gets to deal toxic damage to a target of his choice. It's the same story when Rat deals him irreducible melée damage at the end of his (Rat's) turn. Had some fun plinking away at him that way once. Having both Innervation Rays out helps counteract the damage you'll be taking :).</p>",
