      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>phantaskippy wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Ameena wrote:<br><blockquote>Damage types are Melée, Fire, Sonic, etc. Irreducible is an attribute which can be applied to damage (regardless of type). It mean cards like Fortitude and Ta Moko are of no use, because they reduce damage, so if that hero gets hit with irreducible damage, it ignores their protection. This does make Omni-10 good against Plague Rat, though, if you can get out the Ablative Coating and Reactive Plating Subroutine ASAP :).&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nDoesn't that cause Omni to hit himself if he is infected, or is the return damage optional?\n</blockquote></div>\nThe reactive damage need not go back to the source of the damage, unlike something like Combat Stance.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's what I get for replying without checking the cards.</p>",
